{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 2226 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "8943e6f547745caacf661369000be885d96589b3a9a3a8fbcaf4b30ae41c89ec" :edb/db-before-t 2225 :edb/db-after-t 2226 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535538 50 #inst "2026-10-09T02:03:46.585Z" 13194139535538 true] [17592186152081 1020 #edb/ref 17592186354293 13194139535538 true] [17592186152081 1020 #edb/ref 17592186354307 13194139535538 true] [17592186152082 1020 #edb/ref 17592186354286 13194139535538 true] [17592186152082 1020 #edb/ref 17592186354300 13194139535538 true] [17592186152649 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535538 true] [17592186152649 1100 "Which of the following is equivalent to the integral ${\\int }_{C}5y{e}^{-x}\\text{d}s,$ where $C$ is the section of the curve $y={e}^{x}$ for $\\,0\\le x\\le e?$" 13194139535538 true] [17592186152649 1100 "Which of the following is equivalent to the integral $∫_(C)5ye^{-x}ds$, where $C$ is the section of the curve $y = e^{x}$ for $0 \\le x \\le e$?" 13194139535538 false] [17592186152649 1145 "Notice that the given curve is of the form $y=y(x).$ Therefore, by setting $x=t,$ we have $y=y(t)={e}^{t}.$ This gives the following parametrization of the curve:\n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨t,{e}^{t}⟩,\\,0\\le t\\le e\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t})j \\\\  & =i+{e}^{t}\\,j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+({e}^{t})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+{e}^{2t}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=5y{e}^{-x}$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =5{e}^{t}\\cdot {e}^{-t}=5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{e}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{e}5\\cdot \\sqrt{1+{e}^{2t}}\\cdot \\text{d}t \\\\  & =5{\\int }_{0}^{e}\\sqrt{1+{e}^{2t}}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535538 true] [17592186354286 1017 #edb/ref 17592186354287 13194139535538 true] [17592186354286 1089 "q-148199" 13194139535538 true] [17592186354286 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535538 true] [17592186354286 1100 "Which of the following is equivalent to the integral ${\\int }_{C}({x}^{3}-2y)\\text{d}s,$ where $C$ is the section of the curve $y=2-\\frac{x}{2}$ for $\\,0\\le x\\le 2?$" 13194139535538 true] [17592186354286 1113 #uuid "e7d9bec2-9225-5625-8a03-8734f22a69ef" 13194139535538 true] [17592186354286 1145 "Notice that the given curve is of the form $y=y(x).$ Therefore, by setting $x=t,$ we have $y=y(t)=2-\\frac{t}{2}.$ This gives the following parametrization of the curve:\n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨t,2-\\frac{t}{2}⟩,\\,0\\le t\\le 2\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2-\\frac{t}{2})j \\\\  & =i-\\frac{1}{2}\\,j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{(-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+\\frac{1}{4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)={x}^{3}-2y$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & ={t}^{3}-2(2-\\frac{t}{2})={t}^{3}+t-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}({t}^{3}+t-4)\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}\\cdot \\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}({t}^{3}+t-4)\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535538 true] [17592186354287 1000 #edb/ref 17592186354288 13194139535538 true] [17592186354287 1000 #edb/ref 17592186354289 13194139535538 true] [17592186354287 1000 #edb/ref 17592186354290 13194139535538 true] [17592186354287 1000 #edb/ref 17592186354291 13194139535538 true] [17592186354287 1000 #edb/ref 17592186354292 13194139535538 true] [17592186354287 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535538 true] [17592186354287 1041 "selection" 13194139535538 true] [17592186354287 1104 #edb/ref 17592186354292 13194139535538 true] [17592186354287 1110 #uuid "5ad41713-dc73-5809-a709-9c4f3e5db871" 13194139535538 true] [17592186354288 1034 "\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}({t}^{3}-t-4)\\,\\text{d}t" 13194139535538 true] [17592186354288 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535538 true] [17592186354288 1111 #uuid "6ad4d858-3000-5bff-b917-1e12db16be3f" 13194139535538 true] [17592186354289 1034 "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(t-4)\\,\\text{d}t" 13194139535538 true] [17592186354289 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535538 true] [17592186354289 1111 #uuid "13a19305-67d3-5257-9446-de9aeede780a" 13194139535538 true] [17592186354290 1034 "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(2{t}^{3}+t-8)\\,\\text{d}t" 13194139535538 true] [17592186354290 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535538 true] [17592186354290 1111 #uuid "441373ef-aec4-5773-b1fb-9ca34d53726a" 13194139535538 true] [17592186354291 1034 "\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}({t}^{3}+2t-8)\\,\\text{d}t" 13194139535538 true] [17592186354291 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535538 true] [17592186354291 1111 #uuid "a972e739-468a-5bcc-8fa0-cab0fa633b86" 13194139535538 true] [17592186354292 1034 "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}({t}^{3}+t-4)\\,\\text{d}t" 13194139535538 true] [17592186354292 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535538 true] [17592186354292 1111 #uuid "734edcef-4ff5-5c8c-a578-bd3b2af64a5d" 13194139535538 true] [17592186354293 1017 #edb/ref 17592186354294 13194139535538 true] [17592186354293 1089 "q-148216" 13194139535538 true] [17592186354293 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535538 true] [17592186354293 1100 "Evaluate the integral of the function $f(x,y)=x+y$ along the line $y=x,$ $\\,0\\le x\\le 3.$" 13194139535538 true] [17592186354293 1113 #uuid "b7886d41-4806-56c1-89bc-cb400226a219" 13194139535538 true] [17592186354293 1145 "Notice that the given curve is of the form $y=y(x).$ Therefore, by setting $x=t,$ we have $y=y(t)=t.$ This gives the following parametrization of the curve:\n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨t,\\,t⟩,\\,0\\le t\\le 3\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(u) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)j \\\\  & =i+\\,j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=x+y$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =t+t=2t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}2t\\cdot \\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\text{d}t \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3}t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\,{t}^{2}{|}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}({3}^{2}-{0}^{2}) \\\\  & =9\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535538 true] [17592186354294 1000 #edb/ref 17592186354295 13194139535538 true] [17592186354294 1000 #edb/ref 17592186354296 13194139535538 true] [17592186354294 1000 #edb/ref 17592186354297 13194139535538 true] [17592186354294 1000 #edb/ref 17592186354298 13194139535538 true] [17592186354294 1000 #edb/ref 17592186354299 13194139535538 true] [17592186354294 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535538 true] [17592186354294 1041 "selection" 13194139535538 true] [17592186354294 1104 #edb/ref 17592186354298 13194139535538 true] [17592186354294 1110 #uuid "ae993687-e497-55c3-bda5-198b267a59ea" 13194139535538 true] [17592186354295 1034 "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{9}" 13194139535538 true] [17592186354295 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535538 true] [17592186354295 1111 #uuid "2fe6dd4d-0594-5aff-a0c5-227124f455e8" 13194139535538 true] [17592186354296 1034 "9" 13194139535538 true] [17592186354296 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535538 true] [17592186354296 1111 #uuid "7173092c-6f04-5a20-ac7c-dc4bf5ffb277" 13194139535538 true] [17592186354297 1034 "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3}" 13194139535538 true] [17592186354297 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535538 true] [17592186354297 1111 #uuid "242d0712-f06b-5629-bbd4-3b3d9c310f5e" 13194139535538 true] [17592186354298 1034 "9\\sqrt{2}" 13194139535538 true] [17592186354298 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535538 true] [17592186354298 1111 #uuid "709f7147-b47d-5122-a184-79102b65373d" 13194139535538 true] [17592186354299 1034 "3\\sqrt{2}" 13194139535538 true] [17592186354299 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535538 true] [17592186354299 1111 #uuid "2d93ff20-1e1b-5ece-b19b-b8d2d6131851" 13194139535538 true] [17592186354300 1017 #edb/ref 17592186354301 13194139535538 true] [17592186354300 1089 "q-76415" 13194139535538 true] [17592186354300 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535538 true] [17592186354300 1100 "Which of the following is equivalent to the integral ${\\int }_{C}y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}s,$ where $C$ is the section of the curve $y=2{x}^{2}$ between the points $(1,2)$ and $(3,18)?$" 13194139535538 true] [17592186354300 1113 #uuid "05201083-bb4f-5259-a034-25bea0f3366d" 13194139535538 true] [17592186354300 1145 "Notice that the given curve is of the form $y=y(x).$ Therefore, by setting $x=t,$ we have $y=y(t)=2{t}^{2}.$ This gives the following parametrization of the curve:\n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨t,2{t}^{2}⟩,\\,1\\le t\\le 3\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{2})j \\\\  & =i+4t\\,j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(4t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+16{t}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =2{t}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}2{t}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\cdot \\sqrt{1+16{t}^{2}}\\cdot \\text{d}t \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{1}^{3}{t}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,\\sqrt{1+16{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535538 true] [17592186354301 1000 #edb/ref 17592186354302 13194139535538 true] [17592186354301 1000 #edb/ref 17592186354303 13194139535538 true] [17592186354301 1000 #edb/ref 17592186354304 13194139535538 true] [17592186354301 1000 #edb/ref 17592186354305 13194139535538 true] [17592186354301 1000 #edb/ref 17592186354306 13194139535538 true] [17592186354301 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535538 true] [17592186354301 1041 "selection" 13194139535538 true] [17592186354301 1104 #edb/ref 17592186354302 13194139535538 true] [17592186354301 1110 #uuid "756470d7-6a29-59b7-8494-67363a155edf" 13194139535538 true] [17592186354302 1034 "2{\\int }_{1}^{3}{t}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,\\sqrt{1+16{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t" 13194139535538 true] [17592186354302 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535538 true] [17592186354302 1111 #uuid "4cea0e19-33d9-58c8-9038-f6beb23ba941" 13194139535538 true] [17592186354303 1034 "2{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,\\sqrt{1+16{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t" 13194139535538 true] [17592186354303 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535538 true] [17592186354303 1111 #uuid "15fef846-3de1-5b77-b28a-e928d62653c7" 13194139535538 true] [17592186354304 1034 "{\\int }_{1}^{3}{t}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,\\sqrt{1+4{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t" 13194139535538 t